<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Igor of Kiev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">?–945</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Igor I of Kiev</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Igor was the ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a> from about 912 to 945, called in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik">Rurik</a>. He led raids on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 941 and 944, the first ending in defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-fire">Greek fire</a>, and concluded a trade treaty with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>. In 945 he was killed by the Drevlians when he tried to collect a second tribute from them.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/igor-of-kiev.jpg" alt="Igor of Kiev" width="134" height="283" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Igor_RC.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
